{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Fourth plan review 2026-10-18 (BLOCK, 1 move): the CI-run test inventory was confined to `tests/unit` and four files. Confirmed: CI runs `pytest -m 'not integration and not external'` over the whole tree, so `tests/interfaces/*` executes too. Full inventory built on origin/main b97d414b8e2 (code unchanged at 3beb7e4 for these files) with two greps, which AC2 now names verbatim.\n\nGrep A, removed verbs as string literals in any quoting (`['\"](check-ac|clarity-check|quality-check|get-file-impact|get-verify-commands|list-descendants|session-logs|untag)['\"]`, plus `tag`/`exists`/`format` as CLI argv), tests and scripts, excluding the two registry/dispatch tests that enumerate the removed set by design:\n\n- `scripts/probe_rebar.py:321-323` (untag), `:396-403` (clarity-check, check-ac x2, quality-check x2), `:413-414` (get-file-impact), `:419-420` (get-verify-commands), `:468-469` (list-descendants), `:489,492` (check-ac, quality-check json)\n- `scripts/retarget_jira_project.py:130` (untag subprocess)\n- `scripts/gen_cli_reference.py:131` (`MUTATION_VERBS[\"untag\"]`, this story edits it)\n- `tests/fixtures/ticket-cli-baseline.json:37` (untag)\n- `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_error_envelope.py:56` (get-verify-commands)\n- `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_schema_coverage.py:97,100,101,106` (session-logs, check-ac, quality-check, get-verify-commands)\n- `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_schema_outputs.py:129,216,217` (list-descendants, check-ac, quality-check)\n- `tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_argparse.py:94` (`main([\"tag\", ...])`)\n- `tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli.py:122` (`_cli(\"tag\", \"-h\")`)\n- `tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_space_form_options.py:49,52` (session-logs --limit both forms)\n- `tests/interfaces/facades/test_file_impact_scope_heldout.py:134` (get-file-impact)\n- `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_criteria_heading_collapse.py:66,67,91,92` (clarity-check, check-ac)\n- `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_exit_codes.py:82,83,138` (check-ac, quality-check, clarity-check)\n- `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_gate_rubric_consistency.py:58,61,69,70` (clarity-check, check-ac)\n- `tests/interfaces/queries/test_recent_session_logs.py:40` (`python -m rebar.cli session-logs`)\n- `tests/unit/test_core_cli_parsers.py:47,49,50,54-57,77` (census rows) and `:150,154` (parametrize)\n- `tests/unit/test_mutation_confirmations.py:135,142,150,152,157,159` (tag/untag) and `:528` (`leaf_confirm(\"tag\", ...)`)\n- `tests/unit/test_cli_body_guard.py:160,165,170` (tag/untag)\n\nGrep B, removed handler symbols imported by tests (`_cmd_session_logs|list_descendants_cli|file_impact_cli|verify_commands_cli|exists_cli|format_cli`):\n\n- `tests/unit/test_reads_cli_uninitialized_store.py:81` (parametrize arm `(\"session-logs\", reads_cli._cmd_session_logs, [])`) and `:152` (`inspect.getsource(reads_cli._cmd_session_logs)`)\n- `tests/unit/test_cli_registry_dispatch.py:150` (`rebar._engine_support.lookups.format_cli` monkeypatch target; becomes `resolve_cli`)\n\nAllowlisted, NOT edited by this story because they name the LIBRARY function `rebar.untag` or the removed set by design: `tests/unit/api_surface_baseline.json:1634`, `tests/unit/mcp_library_parity_manifest.json:855`, `tests/unit/test_cross_session_lib.py:260`, `tests/interfaces/facades/test_surface.py:136`, `test_cli_registry_dispatch.py` removed-spelling rows, `test_cross_session_warn_routes.py`.\n\nDescription updated: Scope now says \"every CI-run test that invokes a removed verb or imports a removed handler\" with this comment as the inventory, and a new AC2 names both greps and the allowlist so the post-edit state is checkable, not inferred."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","even